<title>GERMANY: Traub says bankruptcy proceedings start.</title>
<headline>Traub says bankruptcy proceedings start.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German machine tool-maker Traub AG said on Tuesday bankruptcy proceedings had been initiated, as it had previously indicated was likely following the failure of efforts to scale back debt with creditors.</p>
<p>Traub said in a statement that takeover offers would be considered from Gildemeister AG and Index, two firms that have expressed an interest in the business.</p>
<p>Shares in Traub were earlier suspended by the Stuttgart stock exchange, a move that the Frankfurt bourse said also applied to its market.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
